{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1312447-what-are-boons-from","id":1312447,"title":"What are \"boons\" from?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-05-15T17:10:40-07:00","id":1312447,"title":"What are \"boons\" from?","content":"On the VTR forums I've seen references to &quot;boons&quot; several times. It doesn't appear in a quick search of VTR 1e or 2e core books, so I'm wondering what it's from, and why they matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25307-james_nostack","name":"James_Nostack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T17:28:21-07:00","id":1312452,"title":"","content":"It means a favour. Normally calling one in or promising one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T17:33:10-07:00","id":1312454,"title":"","content":"Boons were a ritualized form of owed favors in <i>Masquerade</i>. They tied into the Prince/sheriff/harpies city style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T17:35:12-07:00","id":1312455,"title":"","content":"The term also came up in the first edition Invictus book. Maybe other places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T17:55:49-07:00","id":1312460,"title":"","content":"Basically what the others have said.<br /> <br /> For old enough vampires, time stops having much meaning, and it doesn't take long to have enough money to live comfortably. So the more useful form of currency is favors from other vampires.<br /> <br /> In some (especially Invictus but others too) cities, these get ritualized to make it harder for people to ignore their debts. Trust is hard to come by in a city full of predators, so if people find out they can't trust your word, you'll start losing allies quickly.<br /> <br /> A &quot;boon&quot; generally refers to a ritualized favor like this. If someone says they owe you a boon, it means they're staking their reputation on being able and willing to pay back the favor whenever you need it. Much more reliable than &quot;I owe you one&quot;.<br /> <br /> --- --- --- --- --- --- --- --- ---<br /> <br /> OOC, the concept came from Masquerade, was carried through without much comment in Requiem 1e, and a lot of people still use it in Requiem 2e. I think the Invictus book has examples of how particular cities enforce them, because the Invictus stereotypically care about these sorts of formal systems more than anyone else. But how much any individual city\u2014or any individual vampire\u2014cares, that's up to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T03:34:55-07:00","id":1312523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1312447-what-are-boons-from?p=1312454#post1312454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Boons were a ritualized form of owed favors in <i>Masquerade</i>. They tied into the Prince/sheriff/harpies city style.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's no longer a thing as of Requiem 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T04:10:41-07:00","id":1312528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1312447-what-are-boons-from?p=1312523#post1312523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So it's no longer a thing as of Requiem 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you count Invictus Oaths as boons because they're ritualized promises, there's nothing for it in 2nd edition. I don't count them as boons because the mechanics reward one party or the other for breaking their oath to fuck over the other side, which is antithetical to the concept of employing a system to ensure someone keeps their word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T04:57:40-07:00","id":1312919,"title":"","content":"What i did with blood contract is to make it work like a blood bond but to certain kind of action for example:<br /> <br /> Prince Maxwell from chicago signs a blood contract with the Gangrel Primogen that gives her right to a domain in the docks as long as she doesnt claim more domain for the next 200 years<br /> <br /> If one of them were to break their promises then he will have to pay 1 WP to act against the contract for a scene and in case of succed make a degneration check.No matter what happens if the contract is broken the one who does gets to bear the mark of the Oathbreaker TM suffering 3 levels of agg damage putting them in disavantadge should the other part choose to take actions","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-20T05:45:05-07:00","id":1313282,"title":"","content":"You could possibly draw influence from the John Wick movies and their &quot;boons&quot; being in the form of gold coins.<br /> <br /> reference: <a href=\"https://john-wick.fandom.com/wiki/Gold_Coin\" target=\"_blank\">https://john-wick.fandom.com/wiki/Gold_Coin</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}